Wave 2 ledger: about 25 candidates screened, 9 promising documents opened or inspected, 6 accepted units, 4 direct-fetch blockers/timeouts on UN/ICJ pages, and the rest duplicates or out of scope. The main new mechanisms are UN legal condemnation, Russia’s UN-blocking role, a rejected peace off-ramp, and the Black Sea grain corridor as the clearest cooperative exception.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Allegations of Genocide under the Convention on the Prevention and Punishment of the Crime of Genocide (Ukraine v. Russian Federation), Order of 16 March 2022","publisher":"International Court of Justice","publication_date":"2022-03-16","url":"https://www.icj-cij.org/node/106135","claim":"The ICJ found Ukraine had a plausible right not to be subjected to Russian military operations under the claimed genocide-prevention rationale and ordered Russia to immediately suspend the military operations it commenced on 24 February 2022.","locator":"paragraphs 60, 74, and operative clause 86","source_type":"legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary international court order with direct legal findings and binding provisional measures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-period 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Putin's launched invasion and Russia's wartime justification for it.","contrary_evidence":["Russia disputed the court's framing and the order did not reach the merits of the case."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.3","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Security Council Calls Emergency Special Session of General Assembly on Ukraine Crisis, Adopting Resolution 2623 (2022) by 11 Votes in Favour, 1 Against, 3 Abstentions","publisher":"United Nations Security Council","publication_date":"2022-02-27","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/sc14809.doc.htm","claim":"The Security Council, after Russia voted against resolution 2623, called an emergency special session of the General Assembly on the Ukraine crisis because the Council's permanent members lacked unanimity on Russia's actions.","locator":"headline and lead paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UN Security Council press release summarizing a recorded vote and its procedural consequence.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-period 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Russia's veto role is directly attributable to Putin's government as the permanent member represented in the Council.","contrary_evidence":["The result is procedural rather than a merits ruling, so it primarily shows obstruction of UN peace action rather than a substantive judgment."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"General Assembly Overwhelmingly Adopts Resolution Demanding Russian Federation Immediately End Illegal Use of Force in Ukraine, Withdraw All Troops","publisher":"United Nations General Assembly","publication_date":"2022-03-02","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/ga12407.doc.htm","claim":"The General Assembly demanded that Russia immediately end its invasion of Ukraine, unconditionally withdraw all forces, reverse its February 21 decision on the Donetsk and Luhansk regions, and allow humanitarian access and civilian protection.","locator":"headline and lead paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UN General Assembly press release summarizing the adopted resolution and vote.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-period 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Putin's invasion and subsequent escalation posture.","contrary_evidence":["The resolution was nonbinding, so it is evidence of international rejection rather than enforced compliance."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"With 143 Votes in Favour, 5 Against, General Assembly Adopts Resolution Condemning Russian Federation’s Annexation of Four Eastern Ukraine Regions","publisher":"United Nations General Assembly","publication_date":"2022-10-12","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/ga12458.doc.htm","claim":"The General Assembly condemned Russia's attempted annexation of Donetsk, Kherson, Luhansk, and Zaporizhzhia and demanded that Russia immediately withdraw and reverse those decisions.","locator":"headline and lead paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UN General Assembly press release on a recorded vote and resolution text.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-period 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Putin's annexation decisions.","contrary_evidence":["The resolution is nonbinding, but it remains strong evidence of international legal and political repudiation."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"General Assembly Adopts Text Recommending Creation of Register to Document Damages Caused by Russian Federation Aggression against Ukraine, Resuming Emergency Special Session","publisher":"United Nations General Assembly","publication_date":"2022-11-14","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/ga12470.doc.htm","claim":"The General Assembly recommended creating an international damage register and recognized the need for accountability and reparations for damage caused by Russia's wrongful acts in Ukraine.","locator":"headline and lead paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UN General Assembly press release summarizing the adopted text and vote.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-period 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Putin's war and annexation policy as the underlying conduct being addressed.","contrary_evidence":["The vote concerns accountability after the fact rather than a direct contemporaneous change in conduct."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.9","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Exclusive-As war began, Putin rejected a Ukraine peace deal recommended by his aide: sources","publisher":"Reuters","publication_date":"2022-09-14","url":"https://m.investing.com/news/world-news/exclusiveas-war-began-putin-rejected-a-ukraine-peace-deal-recommended-by-his-aide-sources-2891610?ampMode=1","claim":"Reuters reported that Putin rejected a provisional deal recommended by his envoy Dmitry Kozak that would have removed the need for large-scale occupation, and instead expanded Russia's objectives to include annexation of Ukrainian territory.","locator":"opening paragraphs and later summary of Kozak talks","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters exclusive based on multiple anonymous sources close to the Russian leadership; credible but not independently document-verified.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-period 2022 with retrospective reporting on the invasion period.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributed to Putin's rejection of a negotiated off-ramp.","contrary_evidence":["Kremlin denied the report and Ukraine did not confirm the proposed deal."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.2","2B.3","2B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Joint Coordination Centre opens in Istanbul to facilitate safe export of commercial foodstuffs and fertilizers from Ukrainian ports","publisher":"United Nations in Türkiye","publication_date":"2022-07-28","url":"https://turkiye.un.org/en/192332-joint-coordination-centre-opens-istanbul-facilitate-safe-export-commercial-foodstuffs-and","claim":"Russia, Ukraine, Türkiye, and the UN inaugurated a Joint Coordination Centre in Istanbul to operationalize the Black Sea Grain Initiative and establish a humanitarian maritime corridor for safe exports of grain, foodstuffs, and fertilizers.","locator":"lines 56-66","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary UN press release with concrete implementation details, named participants, and a clear humanitarian purpose.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-period 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Putin's government through Russia's direct participation in the agreement and JCC implementation.","contrary_evidence":["The initiative was a limited humanitarian corridor, not a general shift away from the broader war."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}
